4. Semantic Alignment Between Films

Now take a target film B.

Do not align scenes literally.

Align their functions.

For example:

SOURCE:
small homeland
    ↓
emotional safety
    ↓
simple intimate musical identity
TARGET:
desert farm / spaceship / bedroom / city apartment
    ↓
emotional safety
    ↓
???

The physical objects differ.

The relationship survives.

Therefore:

\text{SOURCE OBJECT}
\neq
\text{TARGET OBJECT}

while:

\boxed{\text{SOURCE RELATION}\approx\text{TARGET RELATION}}

J-Hooks reconstructs the musical response appropriate to the target.

