14. The Bigger Discovery

J-Hooks isn’t ultimately about soundtracks.

It’s a machine for discovering:

\boxed{\text{How one medium knows what another medium is doing.}}

Image and music are different representations.

Yet filmmakers repeatedly create relationships between them that audiences understand.

So mine those relationships.

Then eventually:

\text{visual}
\leftrightarrow
\text{music}
\leftrightarrow
\text{language}
\leftrightarrow
\text{movement}
\leftrightarrow
\text{emotion}
\leftrightarrow
\text{narrative}

J-Hooks becomes another Interface Forge.

It discovers bridges between representational spaces.

